-- title:
--   Good points of the Igusa ∞-branch read non-node places (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=3$ (hypothesis `hq3`), $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. Two function fields occur: $\bar F_{M'} =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside Laurent series, and $\bar F =$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of level $q^2M'$ with the subgroup `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, that is the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts $\bar F_{M'} \le \bar F$. On the reduction side, $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`: those $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the geometric $j$-generator lies in `ssJSet q κ`, the set of $j \in \kappa$ such that every elliptic curve over $\kappa$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ with ambient field $\bar F_{M'}$ and residue field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\bar F_{M'}$ meeting the constants exactly in $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with $A \to \kappa$ on constants, every nonzero element becoming integral with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant, together with a map on places preserving degrees and transporting order divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\bar F_{M'}$, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Further data: $\zeta$ an element of `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}} =$ `OIg` of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), the projective line over $\mathbb Z/q$; and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}} =$ `OSS` of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ indexed by $W$. The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, that $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ (for `lineInfty q`, the point $[1:0]$) is the Gauss ring, consisting of those $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$, the reduction of $y$ nonzero, with $f \cdot y = x$; `hIg`, that every line $\ell$ is $\mathrm{red}_q(\gamma) \cdot \infty$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, that $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; and `hIg_perm`, that for every primitive root $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is permuted by pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ`. The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that a constant lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` regular at every place of $\bar F_{M'}$ at which the coefficient image of `jq` is regular, if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   Next, $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ with ambient field $\bar F$ and residue field `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` (a valuation subring with surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, meeting the constants in $A$, compatible with $A \to \kappa$, and with the scaling property), subject to `hR`: `R.integers` $= O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$; and `hR₀O`: an element of $\bar F_{M'}$ lies in `R₀.integers` precisely when its image in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   The arithmetic of the base is given by: $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$; a subfield $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), henselian (`hhens`), with algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0 \cap A$ (`hκ`); an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ with $A_1 = A \cap K_1$ (`hA₁`), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for $\bar F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$, and quantifies as follows. Let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of $k_0$ in $\bar F$ such that: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by all constants from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\bar F$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and every element of $\bar F$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`) belongs to $F_0$. Put $T_1$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $\bar F$ generated by the image of $K_1$. Let $T_1$ carry any $A_1$-algebra structure whose structure map is the inclusion of $A_1 \subseteq K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ into $\bar F$, let $j_1 \in T_1$ be the element whose image in $\bar F$ is the inclusion of the coefficient image of `jq`, and assume $j_1 \ne 0$. Let $N_{\mathrm{Ig}} =$ `NIg` be a finite set of places of `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to that field such that every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` has its image in `R.integers` with $R$-residue $j$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, and such that $Q \in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ holds exactly when there is $s \in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ is in that of $Q$, for all $g$; thus $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is the set of places of the Igusa residue field lying under the supersingular places.
--
--   On the scheme $\mathfrak X_1 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two charts $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ and $X_{\infty} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, the statement introduces the following predicates. `InStalk x f`, for $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in T_1$: for every point $y$ of either chart mapping to $x$ under `ιFin` respectively `ιInf` there are chart elements $g,h$ with $h \notin y$ and $fh = g$ in $T_1$. `InMax x f`: the same with the extra requirement $g \in y$. `Centred P x`, for a place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: $P$ is rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ if and only if `InMax x f`; this predicate is introduced in the statement but does not occur in its conclusion. `GoodPt x`: the map `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; the only $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ is $x$ itself; every chart element (in either chart) whose image in $\bar F$ is a nonunit of `R.integers` lies in the prime of any chart point over $x$; and for every chart point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1) \notin$ [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7). `Reads x Q`, for a place $Q$ of the Igusa residue field: every $f$ with `InStalk x f` has its image in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and that residue is a nonunit there exactly when `InMax x f`. `OffBranch x`: for every line $\ell \ne \infty$ and every chart point $y$ over $x$ in either chart there is a chart element $b \notin y$ whose image in $\bar F$ is a nonunit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$.
--
--   The asserted conclusion is the conjunction of three statements. First, for every $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x`: there exists a place $Q$ with `Reads x Q`; any two places read by $x$ coincide; and every place read by $x$ lies outside $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. Second, if $x$ and $x'$ both satisfy `GoodPt` and both read the same place $Q$, then $x = x'$. Third, for every place $Q$ of the Igusa residue field with $Q \notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ there exists $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x`, `OffBranch x` and `Reads x Q`.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ case of the dictionary between the good closed points of the two-chart integral model of the level field and the places of the Igusa residue field that are not nodes, established by assembling existence, uniqueness, non-nodality, injectivity and surjectivity of the reading map from the five corresponding statements for $q = 3$. It feeds the construction of the smooth Igusa base model with prescribed point stalks, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_three), on the Igusa-tower leg of the semistable covering of the modular curve.
